{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1471318-exp-and-age","id":1471318,"title":"Exp and age","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-26T23:27:10-08:00","id":1471318,"title":"Exp and age","content":"I'm making NPCs for an upcoming game of Wr20. Several NPCs are very old Wraiths. One was a crusader, one an old west sheriff. My question is, depending on how long they've been among the restless dead what amount of EXP would it make sense to give them? Just looking for ballpark figures for age to exp ratios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25557-ghostvolta","name":"GhostVolta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T06:37:21-08:00","id":1471329,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure this was in Wr20, but in previous Wraith corebooks it was mentioned a starting character could be anything from just deceased to hundreds of years old. So wraiths might not naturally progress in age as vampires for instance do. I'd just give your NPCs stats based on what make sense depending on how they spent their life and afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T20:00:05-08:00","id":1471374,"title":"","content":"Sounds good, thank you for the response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25557-ghostvolta","name":"GhostVolta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T13:04:18-08:00","id":1471450,"title":"","content":"TBH I'd just use basic starting character dots, and then add a few more dots to represent random skills an old ghost may have picked up along the way, perhaps an extra Ability dot or two to show they've improved a little overall. I wouldn't go nuts, though: a couple one-level skills/talents to show something they learned a hundred years ago, or a few one dot knowledges. A couple more backgrounds than usual could represent a century or two of social ties.<br /> <br /> I find it important to remember that just because someone has lived 200 years doesn't mean they're an expert in everything. Just ask old-timers who retired ten years ago, or what not, and are rusty on a number of previous skills. It's tough to stay sharp at more than a few professions because there's only so many hours in a day, whether you're alive or dead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","user":"Callishka","date":". 04-04-2022, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T21:00:46-08:00","id":1471713,"title":"","content":"So I have 3 NPCs that are very vital to the story and are \u201chigh ranking\u201d specialized reapers for the Grim Legion. They are on a mission at the start of the game and have been sent by the Smiling Lord to the site of a mass murder to retrieve the soul of a notorious killer.<br /> Due to the nature of who these NPCs are, and how long they\u2019ve been dead I\u2019m going to make their character sheets up as normal then give them 15 to 20 exp to spend to represent their time spent working for the Smiling Lord. <br /> Im not wanting to go overboard, but right from the outset of the game they are going to be protecting the PCs and helping them navigate being recently deceased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25557-ghostvolta","name":"GhostVolta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T07:31:30-08:00","id":1471776,"title":"","content":"Since this is very much a function of how powerful the wraith started, how active they've been, and how much Oblivion has worn away at them, I think you've got a lot of room to maneuver here. I think your 15 to 20 XP works as well as anything else. You could probably also cash in dots in Passions or Corpus for extra XP if you feel the need.<br /> <br /> I once ran a game with a 500 year old wraith who was slumbering in his fetter (a castle) when it was disassembled and moved to America. That was our explanation for why he lost so much of his power. It was pure narrative convenience, but that game was never going to get into the metaphysics of fetters, so it worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}